    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n16007" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀρχι-συνάγωγος</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾰ],
				ὁ,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>ruler of a synagogue,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ev.Marc.
				5.22
			</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				14.2304
			</span></i>, Ramsay <i>Cities and Bishoprics</i> No.<i><span class="en">
				559
			</span></i>:—hence <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀρχι-συνᾰγωγέω</span></b> , <i><span class="en">
				<u>BCH</u>
				8.463
			</span></i> (Thessalonica, <span class="entity">ii A. D.</span>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>master of a guild</i> or <i>company,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				IGRom.
				1.782
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Thrace</span>), etc.</div>
